  "bug_report_content": "{\"id\":644,\"status\":\"Fixed\",\"summary\":\"Simple \\\"Whitespace only\\\" compression removing \\\"each\\\" keyword from \\\"for each (var x in arr)\\\" loop\",\"labels\":[\"Type-Defect\",\"Priority-Medium\"],\"stars\":0,\"commentCount\":3,\"comments\":[{\"id\":0,\"commenterId\":1134613805571762776,\"content\":\"\\u003cb\\u003eWhat steps will reproduce the problem?\\u003c/b\\u003e\\nSee below code snippet before after compression\\r\\n\\r\\n---Before---\\r\\ncontactcenter.screenpop.updatePopStatus \\u003d function(stamp, status) {\\r\\nfor each ( var curTiming in this.timeLog.timings ) {\\r\\nif ( curTiming.callId \\u003d\\u003d stamp ) {\\r\\ncurTiming.flag \\u003d status;\\r\\nbreak;\\r\\n}\\r\\n}\\r\\n};\\r\\n---After---\\r\\ncontactcenter.screenpop.updatePopStatus\\u003dfunction(stamp,status){for(var curTiming in this.timeLog.timings)if(curTiming.callId\\u003d\\u003dstamp){curTiming.flag\\u003dstatus;break}};\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n\\u003cb\\u003eWhat is the expected output? What do you see instead?\\u003c/b\\u003e\\n---each keyword should be preserved\\r\\n\\r\\n\\u003cb\\u003eWhat version of the product are you using? On what operating system?\\u003c/b\\u003e\\n\\u003cb\\u003ePlease provide any additional information below.\\u003c/b\\u003e\\nfor each (** in **) ---\\u0026gt;  returns object value\\r\\nfor (** in **) --\\u0026gt; returns index\\r\\n\",\"timestamp\":1327042447,\"attachments\":[]},{\"id\":1,\"commenterId\":-5060162230523776870,\"content\":\"\\\"for each\\\" is not part of the EcmaScript standard: https://developer.mozilla.org/en/JavaScript/Reference/Statements/for_each...in\\r\\n\\r\\nIt should however be a parse error.\",\"timestamp\":1327088583,\"attachments\":[]},{\"id\":2,\"commenterId\":-7699928860083865744,\"content\":\"This issue was closed by revision r1737.\",\"timestamp\":1327334272,\"attachments\":[]}]}",
  "fix_diff": "--- com.google.javascript.jscomp.parsing.IRFactory (buggy)\n+++ com.google.javascript.jscomp.parsing.IRFactory (fixed)\n@@ -565,8 +565,15 @@\n \n     @Override\n     Node processForInLoop(ForInLoop loopNode) {\n+      if (loopNode.isForEach()) {\n+        errorReporter.error(\n+            \"unsupported language extension: for each\",\n+            sourceName,\n+            loopNode.getLineno(), \"\", 0);\n \n         // Return the bare minimum to put the AST in a valid state.\n+        return newNode(Token.EXPR_RESULT, Node.newNumber(0));\n+      }\n       return newNode(\n           Token.FOR,\n           transform(loopNode.getIterator()),"
}